                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/sims_speculum_03.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A. Double-ended Sims' speculum"
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Has two blades, usually of different sizes.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "The operator selects the end that provides appropriate exposure.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Common in examination and teaching settings.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/sims_speculum_04.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "B. Single-ended vaginal retractor"
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Has one principal working blade.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Used where a particular blade profile is preferred.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Exact designs vary by manufacturer and surgical purpose.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/sims_speculum_05.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "C. Different blade sizes and curvatures"
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Allow adaptation to patient anatomy and the procedure.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "The appropriate size should provide exposure without unnecessary pressure.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "sims_speculum_subsection_7",
          "subsection_title": "6. Uses and procedures",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "sims_speculum_group_7",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Indication",
                    "Purpose"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Vaginal examination",
                      "Retracts the vaginal wall to expose the vaginal canal."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Cervical examination",
                      "Provides access to inspect the cervix when exposure is adequate."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Vaginal prolapse assessment",
                      "Helps expose the vaginal walls during selected examinations."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Cervical or vaginal biopsy",
                      "Provides visual access for tissue sampling."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Vaginal surgery",
                      "Retracts the vaginal wall to improve operative exposure."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Selected gynaecological procedures",
                      "Facilitates access to the cervix or vaginal canal."
                    ]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Examples of procedures in which Sims' speculum or a similar vaginal retractor may be used include selected vaginal repairs, vaginal hysterectomy and cervical procedures. The specific instrument choice depends on the operation and the surgeon's technique."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "sims_speculum_group_8",
              "group_title": "Important clinical distinction",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Sims' speculum is particularly useful for posterior vaginal wall retraction, but it is not self-retaining. Continuous manual control is required."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "sims_speculum_subsection_8",
          "subsection_title": "7. Advantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "sims_speculum_group_9",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Simple design and straightforward handling.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Provides good posterior vaginal wall retraction.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Available in different blade sizes.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Can be useful when a bivalve speculum does not provide the desired exposure.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Allows the operator to adjust retraction and positioning continuously.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Reusable metal models can be durable and cost-effective.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "sims_speculum_subsection_9",
          "subsection_title": "8. Disadvantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "sims_speculum_group_10",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Requires continuous manual holding.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Occupies one of the examiner's hands.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "May provide less convenient exposure for procedures requiring both hands.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Excessive pressure can cause discomfort or mucosal trauma.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Correct positioning may require practice.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Exposure may be inadequate in some anatomical situations without additional retractors or assistance.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "sims_speculum_subsection_10",
          "subsection_title": "9. Complications and prevention",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "sims_speculum_group_11",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Complication",
                    "Prevention"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Vaginal mucosal abrasion",
                      "Insert and position gently."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Pain or discomfort",
                      "Explain the procedure, select the appropriate size and monitor the patient's response."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Bleeding",
                      "Avoid excessive pressure and unnecessary contact."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Pressure injury",
                      "Do not maintain excessive retraction force or pressure for prolonged periods."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Inadequate exposure",
                      "Adjust positioning or use an alternative or additional retractor."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Cross-infection",
                      "Use appropriate cleaning and validated sterilisation for reusable instruments."
                    ]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "If significant pain, unexpected bleeding or suspected injury occurs, stop and reassess."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "sims_speculum_subsection_11",
          "subsection_title": "10. How to use Sims' speculum in an OSCE",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "sims_speculum_group_12",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/sims_speculum_06.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Step 1 — Preparation"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Introduce yourself, confirm identity, explain the examination, obtain consent, provide privacy and arrange a chaperone according to local policy. Perform hand hygiene and prepare the instrument."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Step 2 — Instrument selection"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Inspect the instrument for damage and select a suitable blade size. Identify the curved blade and handle."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Step 3 — Insertion and positioning"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "With the patient appropriately positioned, introduce the blade gently and position it to retract the intended vaginal wall, commonly the posterior wall. Avoid forceful insertion."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Step 4 — Examination"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Maintain controlled manual retraction and inspect the vaginal walls and cervix as indicated. Obtain samples or assist with the planned procedure if required."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/sims_speculum_07.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Step 5 — Withdrawal and aftercare"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Release retraction gradually and withdraw the instrument gently. Check patient comfort, dispose of or reprocess the instrument correctly, and document the findings."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "sims_speculum_subsection_12",
          "subsection_title": "11. Sims' versus Cusco's speculum",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "sims_speculum_group_13",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Feature",
                    "Sims' speculum",
                    "Cusco's speculum"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Design",
                      "Curved retractor, often double-ended",
                      "Two opposing blades"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Self-retaining",
                      "No",
                      "Usually yes"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Locking mechanism",
                      "Not a standard feature",
                      "Usually present"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Main action",
                      "Retracts a vaginal wall",
                      "Separates opposing vaginal walls"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Manual holding",
                      "Required",
                      "Usually not required once locked"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Typical advantage",
                      "Controlled, targeted retraction",
                      "Hands-free exposure"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Common limitation",
                      "Occupies one hand",
                      "May not provide ideal exposure in every patient"
                    ]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Memory aid: Sims = single-wall retraction; Cusco = two blades that open and lock."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "This is a functional memory aid, not a strict rule about every manufacturer's design."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "sims_speculum_subsection_13",
          "subsection_title": "12. High-yield viva questions",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "sims_speculum_group_14",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q1. Identify this instrument."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Sims' vaginal speculum, a non-self-retaining instrument used to retract the vaginal wall and expose the vaginal canal."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q2. Why is Sims' speculum called non-self-retaining?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It generally requires continuous manual support to maintain the desired retraction."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q3. Which vaginal wall is commonly retracted?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The posterior vaginal wall."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q4. What is its main advantage over Cusco's speculum?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It allows direct, adjustable retraction of a selected vaginal wall and may provide better exposure in particular examinations."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q5. What is its main disadvantage?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It requires continuous manual holding, leaving fewer hands available for other tasks."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q6. Name three complications."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Pain, vaginal mucosal trauma and bleeding."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q7. Can it be used for vaginal surgery?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Yes. It or a similar vaginal retractor may assist with exposure during selected vaginal operations, depending on the procedure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q8. Does it have a screw-locking mechanism?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Not as a standard feature. A screw-locking mechanism is characteristic of typical self-retaining bivalve specula such as Cusco's."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}